  "description": "The WebGpu add-in for CodeBrix.Android applications: the WebGpuRenderView element of the CodeBrix.Platform WebGpu add-in on Android, with the same public API and namespace - a XAML view that hands your code a WebGPU frame (command encoder and texture) on its own Vulkan device, under a continuous, on-demand or manual frame driver, with a SkiaSharp overlay and the CodeBrix.WebGpu sharing contracts and native-module hand-off. Frames reach the screen through the SkiaSharp.Views canvas (Readback, the default) or, with the experimental direct GPU rendering opt-in, through a SurfaceView with no read-back (DirectSurface).",
